                        "form": "tigresses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e1384b77-6e8d-35bc-9bdf-e6da512b7496",
                        "entry_id": "d7fc6a4a-285c-3ed5-a7fb-5e9178b82081",
                        "glosses": [
                            "тигрица"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6057746-bd11-475e-a2c5-6c4b6a8db2cb",
                                "sense_id": "e1384b77-6e8d-35bc-9bdf-e6da512b7496",
                                "text": "Like a savage tigress that tossing in the jungle overlays her own cubs, so the sea dashes even the mightiest whales against the rocks, and leaves them there side by side with the split wrecks of ships.",
                                "translation": "Подобно свирепой тигрице, мечущейся в джунглях, которая способна придушить ненароком собственных детенышей, море выбрасывает на скалы даже самых могучих китов и оставляет их там валяться подле жалких обломков разбитого корабля."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "46e06615-8f05-3a2c-9c07-3cf92816a056",
                        "entry_id": "d7fc6a4a-285c-3ed5-a7fb-5e9178b82081",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. свирепая, жестокая женщина, напоминающая тигрицу"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ab86a67-03f8-4602-b9b9-8e7208a5e19f",
                                "sense_id": "46e06615-8f05-3a2c-9c07-3cf92816a056",
                                "text": "Such is the perversion of that sense among the Chinese at present that probably not one man who reads the Peking Gazette will think there is anything strange in the fact of the Emperor protecting the human tigress who murdered her own son in cold blood."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
